      "code": "from mir_eval.segment import vmeasure\n\n# vmeasure computes the V-measure, which is the harmonic mean of homogeneity and completeness.\n# It takes reference intervals, reference labels, estimated intervals, and estimated labels.\nv_measure, homogeneity, completeness = vmeasure(\n    ref_intervals, ref_labels, est_intervals, est_labels\n)\n\n# The V-measure, homogeneity, and completeness are all bounded between 0.0 and 1.0.\n# Since we are comparing identical inputs (if we were to pass ref to both) it would be 1.0,\n# but here we compare ref and est, so it should be a valid float in [0, 1].\nassert 0.0 <= v_measure <= 1.0, f\"V-measure {v_measure} is out of bounds [0, 1]\"\nassert 0.0 <= homogeneity <= 1.0, f\"Homogeneity {homogeneity} is out of bounds [0, 1]\"\nassert 0.0 <= completeness <= 1.0, f\"Completeness {completeness} is out of bounds [0, 1]\"\n\nprint(f\"__CHECK__ vmeasure {v_measure:.4f}\")",
